      "file_sha256": "5e5d0baa5ca3237dc408525ba39bf73ac2fed7187776bb2a2f463d6caa0c0ce7",
      "code": "- criterion: Defines one shared native BDD declaration model with exact nonempty string IDs, an optional\n    descriptive title, and a nonempty ordered list of nonempty string steps; it preserves step repetition\n    and source text without inferring executable grammar.\n  evidence: specification.native_profile.values and specification.bdd_scenarios define exact IDs, optional\n    descriptive titles, nonempty ordered steps, and the BDD-NATIVE-EXACT-STEPS Given/When/Then case preserves\n    repeated exact step strings.",
      "excerpt_sha256": "5a104f4f2bac9f51338b578fe8791f85513ec21096c71c2b7c22c7b7260234ee"
    },
    "contract_values": {
      "path": "specs/nodes/SG-SPEC-0070.yaml",
      "lines": [
        397,
        399
      ],
      "file_sha256": "5e5d0baa5ca3237dc408525ba39bf73ac2fed7187776bb2a2f463d6caa0c0ce7",
      "code": "    values: id is exact nonempty string; scenario title is optional, but supplied values must be nonempty\n      strings; steps is a nonempty ordered list of nonempty strings. Whitespace-only values are invalid,\n      meaningful strings are not trimmed.",
      "excerpt_sha256": "2592fd6549583b86a5fbdd5b412a0630c886f1e50b90723dded23378158723e6"
    },
